{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"You can install Vue Query via "},{"type":"link","href":"https://npmjs.com","children":[{"type":"text","value":"NPM"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"npm","children":[{"type":"text","value":"NPM"}]},{"type":"code","value":"npm i @tanstack/vue-query","lang":"bash"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"or"}]},{"type":"code","value":"pnpm add @tanstack/vue-query","lang":"bash"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"or"}]},{"type":"code","value":"yarn add @tanstack/vue-query","lang":"bash"},{"type":"blockquote","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Wanna give it a spin before you download? Try out the "},{"type":"link","href":"../examples/basic","children":[{"type":"text","value":"basic"}]},{"type":"text","value":" example!"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Vue Query is compatible with Vue 2.x and 3.x"}]},{"type":"blockquote","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If you are using Vue 2.6, make sure to also setup "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/vuejs/composition-api","children":[{"type":"text","value":"@vue/composition-api"}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"vue-query-initialization","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Vue Query Initialization"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Before using Vue Query, you need to initialize it using "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"VueQueryPlugin"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { VueQueryPlugin } from '@tanstack/vue-query'\n\napp.use(VueQueryPlugin)","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"use-of-composition-api-with-script-setup","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use of Composition API with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"<script setup>"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"All examples in our documentation use "},{"type":"link","href":"https://staging.vuejs.org/api/sfc-script-setup.html","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"<script setup>"}]},{"type":"text","value":" syntax."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Vue 2 users can also use that syntax using "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/antfu/unplugin-vue2-script-setup","children":[{"type":"text","value":"this plugin"}]},{"type":"text","value":". Please check the plugin documentation for installation details."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If you are not a fan of "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"<script setup>"},{"type":"text","value":" syntax, you can easily translate all the examples into normal Composition API syntax by moving the code under "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"setup()"},{"type":"text","value":" function and returning the values used in the template."}]},{"type":"code","value":"<script setup>\nimport { useQuery } from '@tanstack/vue-query'\n\nconst { isLoading, isFetching, isError, data, error } = useQuery({\n  queryKey: ['todos'],\n  queryFn: getTodos,\n})\n</script>\n\n<template>...</template>","lang":"vue"}],"headings":[{"id":"npm","text":"NPM","level":3},{"id":"vue-query-initialization","text":"Vue Query Initialization","level":3},{"id":"use-of-composition-api-with-script-setup","text":"Use of Composition API with <script setup>","level":3}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nYou can install Vue Query via [NPM](https://npmjs.com).\n\n### NPM\n\n```bash\nnpm i @tanstack/vue-query\n```\n\nor\n\n```bash\npnpm add @tanstack/vue-query\n```\n\nor\n\n```bash\nyarn add @tanstack/vue-query\n```\n\n> Wanna give it a spin before you download? Try out the [basic](../examples/basic) example!\n\nVue Query is compatible with Vue 2.x and 3.x\n\n> If you are using Vue 2.6, make sure to also setup [@vue/composition-api](https://github.com/vuejs/composition-api)\n\n### Vue Query Initialization\n\nBefore using Vue Query, you need to initialize it using `VueQueryPlugin`\n\n```tsx\nimport { VueQueryPlugin } from '@tanstack/vue-query'\n\napp.use(VueQueryPlugin)\n```\n\n### Use of Composition API with `<script setup>`\n\nAll examples in our documentation use [`<script setup>`](https://staging.vuejs.org/api/sfc-script-setup.html) syntax.\n\nVue 2 users can also use that syntax using [this plugin](https://github.com/antfu/unplugin-vue2-script-setup). Please check the plugin documentation for installation details.\n\nIf you are not a fan of `<script setup>` syntax, you can easily translate all the examples into normal Composition API syntax by moving the code under `setup()` function and returning the values used in the template.\n\n```vue\n<script setup>\nimport { useQuery } from '@tanstack/vue-query'\n\nconst { isLoading, isFetching, isError, data, error } = useQuery({\n  queryKey: ['todos'],\n  queryFn: getTodos,\n})\n</script>\n\n<template>...</template>\n```\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: installation\ntitle: Installation\n---\n\nYou can install Vue Query via [NPM](https://npmjs.com).\n\n### NPM\n\n```bash\nnpm i @tanstack/vue-query\n```\n\nor\n\n```bash\npnpm add @tanstack/vue-query\n```\n\nor\n\n```bash\nyarn add @tanstack/vue-query\n```\n\n> Wanna give it a spin before you download? Try out the [basic](../examples/basic) example!\n\nVue Query is compatible with Vue 2.x and 3.x\n\n> If you are using Vue 2.6, make sure to also setup [@vue/composition-api](https://github.com/vuejs/composition-api)\n\n### Vue Query Initialization\n\nBefore using Vue Query, you need to initialize it using `VueQueryPlugin`\n\n```tsx\nimport { VueQueryPlugin } from '@tanstack/vue-query'\n\napp.use(VueQueryPlugin)\n```\n\n### Use of Composition API with `<script setup>`\n\nAll examples in our documentation use [`<script setup>`](https://staging.vuejs.org/api/sfc-script-setup.html) syntax.\n\nVue 2 users can also use that syntax using [this plugin](https://github.com/antfu/unplugin-vue2-script-setup). Please check the plugin documentation for installation details.\n\nIf you are not a fan of `<script setup>` syntax, you can easily translate all the examples into normal Composition API syntax by moving the code under `setup()` function and returning the values used in the template.\n\n```vue\n<script setup>\nimport { useQuery } from '@tanstack/vue-query'\n\nconst { isLoading, isFetching, isError, data, error } = useQuery({\n  queryKey: ['todos'],\n  queryFn: getTodos,\n})\n</script>\n\n<template>...</template>\n```\n"}
